  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Consider the number from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>000,</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>001,</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>002</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>998,</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>999</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br />Since, each digit has an equal likelihood of coming and digits used are <math><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br />Hence, 0 appears&nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn></math> times<br />But,&nbsp;<math><mn>000,001,002</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>098,099</mn><mo>;</mo></math><br />have some unwanted zeros, we subtract<br />these zero’s i.e. <math><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>111</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br />Thus, total times 0 appears&nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>111</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>189</mn></math><br />Also, add <math><mn>3</mn></math> zero’s in 1000.<br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mn>189</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>192</mn><mo>.</mo></math>",
    "image": null
  },
